Description: virgl/vtest: serialize whole socket transactions across contexts
 Qt Quick's threaded render loop shares one vtest winsys between contexts.
 Unlocked headers, command bodies, replies and SCM_RIGHTS descriptors interleave,
 causing VTEST_CLIENT_ERROR_COMMAND_ID and a crash in virgl_fence_wait on husky.
 Use the prototype's per-winsys recursive I/O mutex around each complete request
 and reply, including legacy transfer data and blob submit/create pairs. Keep
 it separate from the resource-cache mutex, and destroy it after cache flush.
 Initialize with mtx_plain | mtx_recursive, as the pinned C11 compatibility
 layer rejects mtx_recursive alone.
Origin: other, Rungic M5 route B prototype (.work/husky/m5-B/mesa-vtest-socket-lock.patch)
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-05
